      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW just noticed that actually, if IOMMU is disabled via `iommu\u003doff` or `intel_iommu\u003doff` (and not forced by `platform_optin_force_iommu()` either), we enter `if (no_iommu || dmar_disabled)` and then return -ENODEV rather than 0, so we already ensure failing pKVM initialization in this case?\n\nOTOH, it might still make sense to force panic (via the change in `platform_optin_force_iommu()` I suggested above), since, as you noted in the commit message, \"currently the system doesn\u0027t boot to a healthy state if IOMMU initialization fails while pKVM is enabled\".",
