      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, for no_iommu \u003d 1 or dmar_disabled \u003d 1, we return -ENODEV and since `intel_iommu_init` is called through pKVM, pKVM will fail the initialization and clear the pvmfw memory. So I think this patch is not necessary. What do you think?",
